From: gts7l project
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs35l41: apply Samsung's fsync errata
 (cirrus,use-fsync-errata)

Samsung's driver has cirrus,use-fsync-errata on all four Galaxy Tab S7
amps. Their TDM port runs a short (one BCLK) frame sync, and for that the
driver adds a register patch: VIMON_SPKMON_RESYNC, 0x4310 and
VPVBST_FS_SEL = 0 (already in mainline's revision errata) and
ASP_CONTROL4 = 0x01010000 (missing from mainline).

With the port on stock's short sync (patch 0020 and the DTS) and without
this write, each amp's protection DSP ran a few blocks and then stopped
getting frames: HALO_HEARTBEAT stalled at 6.

Add the ASP_CONTROL4 write as a registered patch when the property is
present, so regcache_sync() re-applies it with the test key unlocked
after hibernation.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l41.c
@@ -1113,6 +1113,19 @@
 #define CS35L41_VIMON_CAL_SUCCESS	2
 #define CS35L41_CAL_SET_STATUS_SET	2
 
+/*
+ * Samsung's driver applies this when DT has cirrus,use-fsync-errata (set on
+ * all four Galaxy Tab S7 amps, whose TDM link uses a one-BCLK short frame
+ * sync). The revision errata (A0 here) already cover VIMON_SPKMON_RESYNC,
+ * 0x4310 and VPVBST_FS_SEL; ASP_CONTROL4 is the missing write. Without it
+ * the DSP stops getting frames (heartbeat stalls) once the port runs short
+ * sync. Registered as a patch, so it is re-applied with the test key
+ * unlocked on every regcache sync (hibernation exit).
+ */
+static const struct reg_sequence cs35l41_fsync_errata_patch[] = {
+	{ CS35L41_ASP_CONTROL4,		0x01010000 },
+};
+
 static void cs35l41_read_calibration(struct cs35l41_private *cs35l41)
 {
 	struct device *dev = cs35l41->dev;
@@ -1492,6 +1505,15 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto err;
 
+	if (device_property_read_bool(cs35l41->dev, "cirrus,use-fsync-errata")) {
+		ret = regmap_register_patch(cs35l41->regmap, cs35l41_fsync_errata_patch,
+					    ARRAY_SIZE(cs35l41_fsync_errata_patch));
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err_probe(cs35l41->dev, ret, "Failed to apply fsync errata\n");
+			goto err;
+		}
+	}
+
 	ret = cs35l41_otp_unpack(cs35l41->dev, cs35l41->regmap);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err_probe(cs35l41->dev, ret, "OTP Unpack failed\n");
